al:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is also coherent: the pre-restart boot identity and healthy directory state were captured, restart was acknowledged, the node became temporarily unreachable, the post-restart identity changed, lifecycle observations independently confirmed that change, persistent data matched its checksum, and writability plus sticky-directory behavior recovered. The only material concern is minor /tmp evidence residue.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle snapshots did not inspect /srv/drop directly, so task-specific state and behavior rely on captured executor commands; the boot-identity transition is independently corroborated by global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity and global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity.","The failed-service lifecycle probe was unsupported because it attempted systemctl on Alpine, so it cannot independently exclude failed OpenRC services (global:after_executor:node1:failed-services). No task-specific service or multi-node cluster was specified; restart recovery is instead demonstrated through resumed platform access, preserved data, and recovered directory behavior."]}
